window.docContents[72].resolve({"/rules/PL1007/#PL1007-configuration":{"contents":"No source option, attribute or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.plumb false and plumb.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Plumb's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; under lake lint a source set_option linter.plumb true turns it back on), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under PL2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL1007: Executable contracts require supported closed evidence","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/PL1007/#PL1007-configuration"},"/rules/PL4004/#PL4004-configuration":{"contents":"There is no name-based allowlist for native proofs; authentication is required for every teaching fence.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL4004: Teaching examples require authenticated compiler classification","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/PL4004/#PL4004-configuration"},"/rules/PL5003/#PL5003-configuration":{"contents":"No source option or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.plumb false and plumb.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Plumb's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; under lake lint a source set_option linter.plumb true turns it back on), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under PL2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nThe rule checks only declarations registered with @[plumb_material] from Plumb.MaterialClaim. Removing a registration from a material declaration changes the reviewed claim, not only this rule's result.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL5003: Registered public material declarations require an Intent section","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/PL5003/#PL5003-configuration"}});